== test: gh35-test-tiers ==
  PASS: auto-detected default declined to sequential WITH a reason (low-core host — legal)
  (sequential host: width assertions below compare against sequential and stay meaningful)
  PASS: --throttle pins 2 workers
  PASS:   and names quiet-CPU + nice in the reason
  PASS: --quiet-cpu is the documented alias of --throttle
  PASS: --burst restores the full-core width (>= balanced default)
  PASS:   and says so in the reason
  PASS: XYZ_VALIDATE_THROTTLE=1 selects the 2-worker quiet mode
  PASS:   and names the env var as the reason
  PASS: XYZ_VALIDATE_MAX_JOBS=3 pins 3 workers
  PASS: a width lever beats a throttle lever in the environment
  PASS: an explicit flag beats the ambient throttle env (flag > env, GH-544 contract)
  PASS: --max-parallel N is the documented alias of --parallel N
  PASS: a throttle flag still overrides XYZ_VALIDATE_PARALLEL=0
  PASS: a malformed XYZ_VALIDATE_MAX_JOBS is refused (exit 2)
  PASS:   and names the variable
  PASS: a malformed XYZ_VALIDATE_THROTTLE is refused (exit 2)
  PASS: --throttle + --burst is a conflict (exit 2), not a silent last-wins
  PASS: --parallel + --sequential is a conflict (exit 2)
  PASS: --tier 9 is refused (exit 2)
  PASS: --tier 2 respects the low-core sequential fallback
  PASS: --tier 2 defaults to the throttled 2-worker pool on an eligible host
  PASS:   and a tier below 3 disclaims promotion evidence in its own header
  PASS: --tier 1 print-mode names tier 1 and disclaims promotion evidence
  PASS: --subsystem hq selects tier 2 and names the subsystem
  PASS: an unknown subsystem is refused (exit 2)
  PASS: --tier 2 --subsystem hq (the ROUTER.md example) works (rc=0)
  PASS: a CONTRADICTING --tier 1 --subsystem hq is refused (exit 2)
  PASS:   and the error says which tier the selector chose
  PASS: every registered suite is in validate.sh's TESTS array (drift: 'none')
  PASS: a registered suite missing from test/ fails the listing loudly (exit 2)
  PASS:   and names the ghost suite
  PASS: tier 1 runs the docs gate and exits green
  PASS:   and really ran the PDDA stub
  PASS:   and ran NO test suite (no 'Running <suite>' banner)
  PASS:   and disclaims promotion evidence
  PASS: a RED docs gate fails tier 1 (exit 1)
  PASS:   and says the documentation gate is RED
  PASS: tier 2 runs the classified subsystem suite and exits green
  PASS:   and really ran the hq stub (marker written by the suite itself)
  PASS:   and ran the identity bracket (tier 2 still runs fixtures)
  PASS:   and disclaims promotion evidence in the tier-2 banner
  PASS:   and the GH-15 summary tallies (no INTERNAL ERROR)
  PASS:   and the static syntax check ran on the changed file
  PASS: the suite worker ran 10 below its caller (caller nice=0, worker nice=10, wanted 10)
  PASS: a RED subsystem suite fails tier 2 (exit 1)
  PASS: --paths-file with an unmapped path refuses (exit 2, fail-closed)
  PASS:   and says which tier it classified as
  PASS: a subsystem with no runnable suites on disk refuses the narrow gate (exit 2)
  PASS:   and the classifier said why: no runnable tests, failing closed
  PASS: a deleted path in the tier-2 list is skipped, not 127'd (exit 0)
  PASS: a changed file with broken bash syntax fails tier 2 (exit 1)
  PASS: docs + subsystem runs the pdda stub in-band (exit 0) and the hq stub in the pool
  PASS: a RED docs gate fails the mixed tier-2 run (exit 1)
  PASS: --auto classifies a docs-only over-upstream diff as tier 1
  PASS: --auto classifies an hq-only diff as tier 2
  PASS: --auto with an unusable range fails closed to tier 3 (zero-path branch or explicit refusal)
  PASS: pre-push hands the push's paths to validate.sh --paths-file (GH-35 dispatch)
  PASS:   and only after the classifier explicitly said tier=2
  PASS: validate.sh --tier 2 exits 2 on a non-tier-2 path list (the hook's fail-closed partner)
  PASS: GH-45: a linked worktree is REFUSED before anything runs (exit 2)
  PASS:   and the message names the real consequence (core.bare)
  PASS:   and names the rest (origin repointed, remote refs deleted, development overwritten)
  PASS:   and names the explicit override
  PASS:   and NOTHING ran — no docs gate, no suite banners
  PASS: GH-45: the override runs the gate AND announces itself (exit 0)
  PASS: GH-45 CONTROL: the normal checkout of the SAME repo still runs the gate (exit 0)
  PASS:   and says nothing about worktrees (silent pass-through)
  PASS: GH-45: ci-local.sh refuses from a linked worktree too (exit 2)
  PASS:   with the same consequence message and override
  PASS: GH-45: an absolute-path invocation whose HERE is the worktree is still refused (exit 2)
  gh35-test-tiers: 70 pass, 0 fail
